  "nl_text": "The database schema named 'rschema_0085' comprises four tables: User, Recipe, Blog, and Collected_Recipe.\nThe User table represents a user of the application. It contains columns for Avatar, Email, Password, Profile, User_ID (as the primary key), and Username. The User_ID is an integer and cannot be null.\nThe Recipe table is used to store information about recipes. It includes columns for Bitter_Level, Calories, Creator_ID (which cannot be null), Ingredients, Large_Image_Filename, Meaty_Level, Number_of_Ratings, Portion, Rating, Recipe_ID (as the primary key), Recipe_Name, Salty_Level, Small_Image_Filename, Sour_Level, Spicy_Level, Steps, Sweet_Level, Total_Time. The Recipe_ID is an integer and cannot be null. The Creator_ID is a foreign key referencing the User_ID in the User table.\nThe Blog table is used to store information about blogs. It includes columns for Author_User_ID (which cannot be null), Blog_ID (as the primary key), Blog_Summary, Blog_Title, and Publication_Time. The Blog_ID is an integer and cannot be null. The Author_User_ID is a foreign key referencing the User_ID in the User table.\nFinally, the Collected_Recipe table is used to store information about which recipes have been collected by which users. It includes columns for Collection_Time, Recipe_ID (which cannot be null), and User_ID (which cannot be null). Both Recipe_ID and User_ID are foreign keys referencing the Recipe_ID and User_ID in their respective tables respectively. The combination of User_ID and Recipe_ID forms the primary key of this table.",
  "gold_question": "The system primarily involves three entities: User (User ID, Username, Email, Password, Profile, Avatar), Recipe (Recipe ID, Recipe Name, Ingredients, Steps, Total Time, Portion, Spicy Level, Bitter Level, Sweet Level, Meaty Level, Salty Level, Sour Level, Rating, Number of Ratings, Large Image Filename, Calories, Creator ID, Small Image Filename), and Blog (Blog ID, Author User ID, Blog Title, Publication Time, Blog Summary). System functionalities include user registration, login, personal information management, recipe publishing, collecting, rating, as well as blog publishing and viewing. Additionally, users can create recipes, collect recipes, and publish blogs, with each recipe and blog being managed by users. The system manages relationships between users and recipes or blogs through creation, collection of recipes, and blog publishing.",
  "input_json": "/data/RSchema_ExpResults4/Experiment2/schema2text_deepseek/0085.json",
  "ddl": "-- Schema for database: rschema_0085\nCREATE TABLE `user` (\n  `user_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `avatar` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `email` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `password` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `profile` text DEFAULT NULL,\n  `username` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`user_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `recipe` (\n  `recipe_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `recipe_name` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `creator_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `ingredients` text DEFAULT NULL,\n  `steps` text DEFAULT NULL,\n  `bitter_level` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `salty_level` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `sour_level` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `spicy_level` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `sweet_level` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `meaty_level` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `calories` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `portion` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `rating` float DEFAULT NULL,\n  `number_of_ratings` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `total_time` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `large_image_filename` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `small_image_filename` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`recipe_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `recipe_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`creator_id`) REFERENCES `user` (`user_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `blog` (\n  `blog_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `author_user_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `blog_title` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `blog_summary` text DEFAULT NULL,\n  `publication_time` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`blog_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `blog_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`author_user_id`) REFERENCES `user` (`user_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `collected_recipe` (\n  `user_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `recipe_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `collection_time` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`user_id`, `recipe_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `collected_recipe_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`user_id`) REFERENCES `user` (`user_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `collected_recipe_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`recipe_id`) REFERENCES `recipe` (`recipe_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;",
